# inc-6fii: make a Human Paladin with the Shield Expert feat and stop in the
# arrival room, saving once so INCURSION_CHAR_PROBE=1 writes logs/charprobe.txt.
#
# The bug: Universal Gear (lib/races.irh) grants a kite shield to any character
# with FT_SHIELD_FOCUS or FT_SHIELD_EXPERT, and the Paladin class kit
# (lib/classes.irh:1651-1652) already grants a kite shield, so a Shield Expert
# paladin ends up with a stack of "2 kite shields". This script builds that
# character so the charprobe sheet can be read.
#
# Reconstructed here from the class-kit scripts (tools/keys/kit-paladin.keys):
# the class kit scripts stop in the arrival room and read INCURSION_KIT_PROBE;
# this one instead saves once, the action that makes INCURSION_CHAR_PROBE write
# logs/charprobe.txt (Game::SaveGame, src/Registry.cpp:1105-1111). Race and
# class are named, not counted; Shield Expert is named on the feat menu.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Athletics"
@choose "Diplomacy"
@choose "Paladin"
@choose "Erich"   # the god the class offers
a       # Attributes: the first offered set
a       # Alignment: the first offered

@choose "Shield Expert"   # the feat the bug needs (needs Shield Proficiency)
@while "Choose a feat" a  # any remaining first-level feats

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

@while "wish to worship" y
@while "personality archetype" a

ESC*3   # dismiss the arrival room description
s*3     # one turn, so the session counts as played

ESC               # System Menu -- NOT a cancel; see load-char-sheet.keys
@expect "System Menu"
b                 # [b] Save and Continue: writes logs/charprobe.txt
@dump:saved
